# jux(rev): a line on the left and the same line backwards on the right.
# Strudel does it in one call; here it is two tracks panned apart, the
# right clip made from the left one through .rev() (#649). In the second
# scene .add([0,2,4]) stacks a triad on each degree before .scale (#650).
# The hats do it too: a drum clip made from a drum clip, steps and all (#653).
tempo 110
scale c minor
track kit drums Tr909 Kit909
track left synth Juno106 JunoPluck
track right synth Juno106 JunoPluck
track hatl drums Tr909 Kit909
track hatr drums Tr909 Kit909
strip left: Level 0.6, Pan -1
strip right: Level 0.6, Pan 1
strip hatl: Level 0.5, Pan -1
strip hatr: Level 0.5, Pan 1

clip beat = kit /16
  bd x...x...x...x...
  cp ....x.......x...
clip hats = hatl /16
  ch x.oxx.o.x3...xo.o
clip stah = hatr hats .rev()
clip fwd = left
  "0 [2 4] <3 5> [~ <4 1>]"
clip back = right fwd .rev()
# Each note a triad of the scale, then the same, backwards, on the right.
clip stack = left .add([0,2,4]) .scale(c4 minor)
  "0 [2 4] <3 5> [~ <4 1>]"
clip stacked = right stack .rev()
scene jux 8: beat hats stah fwd back
scene chords 8: beat hats stah stack stacked
arrange jux chords
